<p>Note: The company said it sold during the second quarter its $3.4 million credit card receivables portfolio and its merchant credit card processor portfolio at an after-tax net gain of about $400,000 or $0.10 per share.</p>
<p>The company also said net income per share reflects a larger increase than net income as a result of 120,100 treasury shares repurchased during the past year that had the effect of increasing net income per share.</p>
<p>Net income was also improved as a result of receiving interest income and recovering legal expenses previously expended on a charged-off commercial loan.</p>
